Sorry to sound like I did.  I was not intending to scold in any way.  It was
just one of faster posts, and I didn't think too much about how I say things.
So, sorry for sounding scoldish...

But, on to the discussion.
I was not trying to say that he was stupid for having what he had, but was
just offering good options.  You are correct in pointing out that what he did
have was a valid combination.  I was just trying to point out some possible
upgrades (again, I admit my tone was cruddy).

The reason that I usually go for Gray dragon scale mail is that it is as good
as the other dragon scale mails, plus it gives an intrinsic that cannot be
gained by eating things, magic protection.  Also, invisibility can be gained
by eating things, as well as disintegration resistance.  I guess it is that I
have never had a problem with black dragons (after the first one which flayed
me with his breath, after that I ate EVERY ONE I could kill, and always got it
by the third try.  Again, this is a percent chance, but for what can be gained
it tends to be worth it).

In effect, I tend to bank on intrinsics a great deal.  I never go to hell w/o
all of the dragon resistances and invisibility.  A cloak of displacement
always makes the first hit miss (except, I believe for certain humans, like
shopkeepers.  This is just from experience, not from the code.  Heck, even the
wizard misses...)
 
Just for the record, I tend to work towards having:
gray dragon scale mail
Hawaiian shirt
cloak of displacement
speed boots
gauntlets of dexterity
Helm of brilliance
shield of reflection
(All, of course, as high + as possible)

From playing too many games of nethack I have come to the conclusion that this
is the best combination, depending, of course, on intrinsics.

But you are right, he did(does) have a very good game going, and I was wrong
in my tone.  I apologize.

